MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_001: Now, how are we going to handle this? Seems like\nno one's available right now...
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_002: Hey, Talimun. Got a problem?
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_003: Ah, Lilian. Excellent timing. I need you to do\nsomething for me.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_004: Who, me? There's money in it, right?
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_005: Negotiating pay before you hear what I have to say?\nGetting ahead of yourself, aren't you?
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_006: Says you. I learned the hard way not to do anything\nwithout terms settled up front.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_007: Last time you said that, we ended up going back\nand forth for hours.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_008: Remember? I needed you to run an errand, and by\nthe time you accepted, the sun was already setting.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_009: Hey, I got there just before sundown. It all worked\nout in the end, so there's no problem.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_010: Anyway, what's the job this time? Another errand?
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_011: This one's a bigger task. I need to get someone\nto appraise a gem I recently acquired, you see...
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_012: But all the appraisers we usually turn to are away.\nWe need someone here and now.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_013: And if I recall, you're a capable appraiser yourself.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_014: Well, I'm not much more than an amateur...but sure,\nI'll do it for a price.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_015: All I'm asking is...this much.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_016: Good luck. You'll get this much, at best.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_017: That's it? Don't be such a cheapskate. But fine, I'll go\ndown to this much.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_018: I've got a company to keep afloat, unfortunately—\nemployees to keep paid, you see...
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_019: Seriously? Come on. You can go a little higher.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_020: Well then. Seems we have a deal. Hope it was worth\nall the time it took.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_021: You brag about being the richest man in Dagda,\nbut you wouldn't know it from how cheap you are.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_022: Vandahl Trading compensates you perfectly well.\nIt's you constantly grumbling!
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_023: If you say so. Just know that the better you pay,\nthe harder I'll try.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_C_024: Hope you're factoring the cost of my wasted time\ninto that little value proposition.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_001: Hehe. Yep. Now this is a proper reward for a job\nwell done.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_002: Hey there, Lilian. Enjoying yourself?
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_003: I just got a pretty sweet payday, so I was countin'\nmy loot. Hehe.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_004: I can see that. I'm asking if you find counting it out\ncoin by coin enjoyable.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_005: You're telling me you don't love money? Some\nmerchant you are.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_006: Of course I love it! But when you've got as much\nas I do, the coins themselves are less interesting.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_007: For me, if I can count them, there are far too few.\nI need gold by the ton to get that thrill anymore.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_008: Which isn't to say I don't enjoy coins. When the light\nhits a mound of gold pieces just right... Incredible.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_009: You said it! Copper coins just don't stack up.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_010: Jewels are easier to carry, but the weight of gold\nreally makes you feel the sense of accomplishment.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_011: I love knowing that something I did had the kind of\nvalue you can hold in your hand.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_012: Yes, exactly! The sparkle of gold makes life\nworth living!
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_013: Here I took you for just another money-grubber, but\nit seems we may get along after all.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_014: Right, then. As a token of friendship, let me give you\na little something that fell into my hands by chance.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_015: It's made of pure gold from the age of Damascar,\nand it's worth a tidy sum.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_016: What?! You're sure you don't mind parting with this?\nDamascar is where my ancestors were from.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_017: Is Talimun the Womanizer trying to woo me with\nexpensive gifts?
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_018: Hahaha! Don't worry. I have no ulterior motive.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_019: I'm simply happy to find another person who shares\nmy sensibilities, you see.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_020: You can think of it as a token of my appreciation\nfor the lovely conversation. If you'll accept...
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_021: Hmm. Alright. I'll accept this as my compensation.\nJust remember one thing!
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_022: I do love expensive stuff, but I'm not the type of girl\nwhose heart can be bought.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_023: I'm glad to hear it. Now, I should say...among those\nwho trade in such curios, this is considered a relic.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_024: It's worth the same as a thousand gold bricks\nof equivalent size. Don't go losing it, eh?
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_025: What?! A thou— I nearly just dropped it out\nof shock!
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_026: Ahaha. I'm sorry. I made up the whole relic bit to see\nhow you'd react... It is pure Damascar gold though.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_027: You may know your jewels, but you still have a lot\nto learn about artifact appraisal, Lilian.
MID_SE_Tal_Lil_B_028: You were teasing me?! Ugh, I'm not getting paid\nenough to deal with you!